Version: 0.0.7.9000
Date: 2026-09-21
R: 4.4.3
Studies: imputation
Note: This is a PARTIAL retention set. Only the imputation ablation was run at
 this version. The coverage, power, bench, mclogit and brms studies were last
 run at 0.0.2.9000 and their findings still stand for the model families that
 existed then, but they do NOT cover anything added at 0.0.3.9000 through
 0.0.7.9000: zero-inflated and hurdle counts, ordered outcomes, beta
 regression, instrumental variables, survey-weighted fits, or mediation. Those
 were each validated against an outside implementation (pscl, ordinal,
 glmmTMB, closed-form 2SLS, survey, the Baron-Kenny product) but have no
 coverage or timing cells. Re-running the full set is hours of compute and has
 not been done.
Note: The imputation ablation is new at this version. Five methods across six
 designs, scored on reconstruction AND on coverage of a downstream coefficient
 after Rubin pooling. It was built to settle whether ilm_lowrank_ncp() picks a
 poor rank, which a single earlier design had suggested. It does not settle
 it: cross-validation is worse than parallel analysis in four cells and
 materially better in one. The selector is unchanged. See
 studies/findings/imputation.md.
Note: Chained equations cannot be fitted at n = 60, p = 80 and does not fail
 fast when asked -- it runs for hours on rank-deficient per-column
 regressions. That cell is recorded as inapplicable rather than attempted.
